abstract: >-
  An early warning system that flags restaurant chain locations at elevated risk of
  closure and explains why using customer review language. It combines a landmark
  two-tier survival model, BERTopic complaint themes, a retrieval-augmented evidence
  assistant, and a three-agent Risk Committee behind a single LLM gateway, served by a
  Streamlit application.
keywords:
  - survival analysis
  - natural language processing
  - BERTopic
  - retrieval augmented generation
  - LLM agents
  - Yelp Open Dataset
license: MIT
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-10-03
